      "refersTo": "search-field",
      "description": "\"¿A qué libro vas?\": ruled search sign with ámbar focus.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-search\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 18 18\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"7.5\" cy=\"7.5\" r=\"5\"/><path d=\"M11.5 11.5L16 16\"/></svg><input placeholder=\"¿A qué libro vas?\"></label>",
      "css": ".ds-search{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:0 12px;border:2px solid #f3f1ea;border-radius:2px;background:#0b1230;color:#a9b3d6;transition:background 140ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)} .ds-search:hover{background:#0f1838} .ds-search:focus-within{outline:2px solid #ffc20e;outline-offset:2px} .ds-search input{flex:1;min-width:0;padding:12px 0;border:0;background:transparent;color:#f3f1ea;caret-color:#ffc20e;font-family:Overpass,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;outline:0} .ds-search input::placeholder{color:#a9b3d6}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status Tags",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "status-tag",
      "description": "Stop state tags: next (porcelain), read (ink), optional detour (dashed ink).",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-next\">Próxima</span> <span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-read\" style=\"--ink:#b07cf0\">Leído</span> <span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-detour\" style=\"--ink:#b07cf0\">Desvío optativo</span>",
      "css": ".ds-tag{display:inline-block;padding:1px 8px;border:1px solid #a9b3d6;color:#f3f1ea;font-family:Overpass,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase} .ds-tag-next{background:#f3f1ea;border-color:#f3f1ea;color:#070c22} .ds-tag-read{background:var(--ink);border-color:var(--ink);color:#070c22} .ds-tag-detour{border-style:dashed;border-color:var(--ink);color:var(--ink)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Route Track (vía gruesa)",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "route-station",
      "description": "Thick vertical track in the route ink with numbered porcelain stations: read, next (dashed ring), and a dashed detour off a siding.",
      "html": "<ol class=\"ds-track\" style=\"--ink:#b07cf0\"><li class=\"ds-stop\" data-state=\"read\"><span class=\"ds-st\">1</span><span class=\"ds-t\">Economics in One Lesson</span></li><li class=\"ds-stop\" data-state=\"next\"><span class=\"ds-st\">2</span><span class=\"ds-t\">Free to Choose</span></li><li class=\"ds-stop ds-detour\"><span class=\"ds-st\">3</span><span class=\"ds-t\">Principles of Economics</span></li></ol>",
      "css": ".ds-track{position:relative;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:40px;font-family:'Big Shoulders','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;color:#f3f1ea} .ds-track::before{content:'';position:absolute;left:18px;top:28px;bottom:28px;width:20px;background:var(--ink)} .ds-stop{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px} .ds-st{position:relative;z-index:1;display:grid;place-items:center;width:56px;height:56px;box-sizing:border-box;border:6px solid var(--ink);border-radius:999px;background:#f3f1ea;color:#070c22;font-size:29px;font-weight:800} .ds-stop[data-state=read] .ds-st{background:var(--ink);border-color:#f3f1ea} .ds-stop[data-state=next] .ds-st{outline:3px dashed #f3f1ea;outline-offset:5px} .ds-detour{padding-left:44px} .ds-detour .ds-st{border-style:dashed;background:#0b1230;color:#f3f1ea} .ds-t{font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tramo a pie Sign",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "",
      "description": "Walked gap: porcelain dotted border on sunken enamel, porcelain footsteps, no line ink.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-walk\"><span class=\"ds-walk-name\">Tramo a pie</span><span class=\"ds-walk-sev\">Fuerte</span><ul><li>Contabilidad básica</li><li>Estadística descriptiva</li></ul></div>",
      "css": ".ds-walk{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto auto 1fr;gap:8px 12px;align-items:center;padding:12px;border:2px dotted #a9b3d6;background:#070c22;color:#f3f1ea;font-family:Overpass,system-ui,sans-serif} .ds-walk-name{font-size:.875rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase} .ds-walk-sev{justify-self:start;padding:0 8px;border:1px solid #a9b3d6;color:#a9b3d6;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase} .ds-walk ul{grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;display:grid;gap:4px;font-size:.875rem;font-weight:600} .ds-walk li{position:relative;padding-left:20px} .ds-walk li::before{content:'';position:absolute;left:3px;top:.55em;width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:#f3f1ea}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Midnight Transit Diagram",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Midnight Transit Diagram\"**\n\nDagerBooks is drawn as a city subway map at night. A deep midnight enamel owns every pixel of ground; porcelain-white stations, rules and signage sit on it like enamel plates in a Buenos Aires station; and twelve saturated line inks, each lettered A–L on a round disc, carry the topics outward from Km 0. Nothing on the surface is a card, a gradient or a glow. Information is posted the way transit authorities post it: square-cornered signs, 2px rules, tracked capitals, numbered stops.\n\nThe world has two scales. On the map (radial Grafo and horizontal Subte) lines are thin strokes, stations are porcelain rings, fare zones are dotted rings, and the chosen line burns while the rest drop to a third of their ink. On reading surfaces (book, topic and route pages) the same vocabulary is enlarged: a route becomes a thick vertical track in its ink with porcelain stations the size of a thumb, and gaps in the catalog are walked, not ridden. Personality comes from the transit metaphor carried all the way down (the \"Lo leí\" button is a ticket you punch, progress is \"Leíste 2 de 3\"), not from ornament.\n\nDensity is a reader setting (compacta, media, aireada), applied as one multiplier over list rows, gaps and line-height. The use scene is a desk at night with a stream on a second monitor; the dark enamel is the v1 commitment, a porcelain variant is deferred.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Midnight enamel ground, porcelain foreground, twelve line inks as the only saturated color.",
      "Lettered line discs A–L wherever a topic is named.",
      "Big Shoulders signage in uppercase; Overpass wayfinding labels in tracked caps.",
      "Square, 2px-ruled rectangles for every interactive sign; circles only for discs and stations.",
      "Dashed and dotted strokes carry meaning: fare zones, optional detours, the next stop, tramos a pie.",
      "Motion is a train run: ease-out-expo, stroke-draw from Km 0, instant under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Third-of-Ink Rule",
        "body": "When a line is chosen it burns at full ink and active stroke width; every other line drops to a third of its ink (opacity 0.32). Selection is never shown with a glow or a new color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Belongs to the Line Rule",
        "body": "Line inks color only line-owned things (tracks, discs, read fills, sign bands, tags of that route). Only two inks hold a second job: ámbar (focus, progress, ticket) and escarlata (service notices).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signage Rule",
        "body": "Display and title text is Big Shoulders uppercase; anything the reader acts on (buttons, tags, nav) is Overpass bold in tracked caps. Body text is never tracked and never uppercase.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Density Dial Rule",
        "body": "Vertical rhythm in lists and panels reads the density-derived spacing, never a fixed step, so compacta / media / aireada stay one setting.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Float-Only Shadow Rule",
        "body": "If it does not float over the map or page, it gets a rule, not a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do pass a line's color to components as `--ink` and let them paint tracks, discs, fills and tags from it.",
      "Do drop unchosen lines to the shared dim opacity (0.32) instead of recoloring them.",
      "Do rule interactive rectangles with a 2px line and a 2px corner, 44px minimum hit area.",
      "Do show optional and incomplete things with dashes (detours, \"por completar\" in ámbar) and walked gaps with porcelain dots.",
      "Do set signage in Big Shoulders uppercase and actions in Overpass tracked caps.",
      "Do route every animation through ease-out-expo and the fast/base/route durations, which collapse to 0 under reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce colors outside enamel, porcelain and the twelve inks, and don't use gradients as fills.",
      "Don't round signs past 2px or turn rectangles into pills; circles are for discs and stations only.",
      "Don't put shadows on anything that does not float.",
      "Don't give a tramo a pie a line ink or warning color; it is porcelain on sunken enamel.",
      "Don't set new text below 0.75rem."
    ]
  }
}